{"id": "EUVD-2026-80435", "enisaUuid": "373cd4ce-2d29-3d75-89cf-29f84aa110ea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: avoid NULL checkpoint thread access in sysfs\n\ncheckpoint_merge can be enabled even when no checkpoint merge thread is\nrunning. A read-only mount is one case: f2fs does not start\nf2fs_issue_ckpt there, but ckpt_thread_ioprio is still writable through\nsysfs.\n\nThe ckpt_thread_ioprio store path updates the saved ioprio value and,\nwhen checkpoint_merge is enabled, calls set_task_ioprio() for the\ncheckpoint thread. If cprc->f2fs_issue_ckpt is NULL, that dereferences a\nNULL task pointer.\n\nProtect ckpt_thread_ioprio sysfs writes with s_umount as well, so the\ncheckpoint thread cannot disappear under the store path while updating\nits ioprio.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22760e3e9cecbddc475edc91600787abf407a302", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6573f3ffc19542de9ebc1a2b1f930fd48ba538c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aefcec3bebdeed2bff444378122300763325ba23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f3b99c50dd0da1777994ce7c7e60d39b9f60f4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cb33b00c8fbb6e8f1fa3d281c3036d5f7c7c41f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89835", "GHSA-2hjf-mqww-7576"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a9b4eff-4494-34ba-9bfb-f0638ba73302", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65920661708b7c0f3db45c9cd5d0095034ee37f <5cb33b00c8fbb6e8f1fa3d281c3036d5f7c7c41f"}, {"id": "17d6b3fb-b47b-34ed-b682-e85628f505fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1ae6fccd-040c-36a6-8f87-5d01468ead27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "3dd29e15-cab7-3f18-b233-5760159fa101", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65920661708b7c0f3db45c9cd5d0095034ee37f <8f3b99c50dd0da1777994ce7c7e60d39b9f60f4b"}, {"id": "4e3c8b57-4176-36dd-bc77-ba99e677d9a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65920661708b7c0f3db45c9cd5d0095034ee37f <22760e3e9cecbddc475edc91600787abf407a302"}, {"id": "54c73713-ff3f-31f5-b85c-f109b32491c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "aed0fca9-f2d0-345c-894c-cae7aba27aee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65920661708b7c0f3db45c9cd5d0095034ee37f <aefcec3bebdeed2bff444378122300763325ba23"}, {"id": "bed68b1e-fc8f-34fc-b544-5401802ea78e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e65920661708b7c0f3db45c9cd5d0095034ee37f <a6573f3ffc19542de9ebc1a2b1f930fd48ba538c"}, {"id": "c6faa27d-69f2-3faa-b7d1-39567b17bafc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "c9296d49-0bd2-3ff3-b04a-488d90f677fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dcf11009-5dd9-3296-94a2-2ef6761c4ac6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ddb4d021-e863-3cd6-9f6e-216373a41096", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "586f2c23-8082-38e8-bee1-e69b8091091c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}